---
description: Figma implementation rule
alwaysApply: true
---

Before implementing any screen or component, inspect the relevant Figma frame using the connected Figma MCP server.

Use Figma for layout, visual hierarchy, component structure, spacing, responsive behavior, and interaction cues.
Use the repo docs for product logic, terminology, entity relationships, statuses, and MVP scope.

Workflow before coding:
1. Identify the route or component being built.
2. Read docs/figma-map.md for the matching Figma frame.
3. Inspect that frame through Figma MCP.
4. Read the relevant docs from docs/product and docs/engineering.
5. Propose a short implementation plan.
6. Code only the requested slice.

Do not guess visual details when the Figma prototype contains the answer.
Do not convert the Figma prototype into a static visual clone. Build reusable components and data structures that match the domain model.
If Figma conflicts with docs/domain-glossary.md or docs/product/domain-model.md, pause and ask before changing product behavior.
